{"id": "EUVD-2026-96560", "enisaUuid": "b8b46fa1-6e83-3e12-8910-f52be110274c", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SysPositionController edit handler that allows any authenticated user to modify organizational positions. Low-privileged attackers can obtain position ids from the unguarded list endpoint and send PUT or POST requests to /sys/position/edit to alter position names, codes, and ranks.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:58:56", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_c090_position_edit.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysPositionController.java#L137-L152", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-position-edit"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108621", "GHSA-8cfj-f246-mwh6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f0cd606-3e64-3cfe-97e5-4ac9c9df9f2e", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "10e3e7f9-43c9-39b3-a8a6-3519c8696213", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}